<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I34614f7b393182f65091b7a5f19ffa7776c2c575" commit="d59fcc0754633a4f452d5d14748da811fd1a060f" commit_message="net: socket ioctl to reset connections matching local address  Introduce a new socket ioctl, SIOCKILLADDR, that nukes all sockets bound to the same local address. This is useful in situations with dynamic IPs, to kill stuck connections.  Signed-off-by: Brian Swetland &lt;swetland@google.com&gt;  net: fix tcp_v4_nuke_addr  Signed-off-by: Dima Zavin &lt;dima@android.com&gt;  net: ipv4: Fix a spinlock recursion bug in tcp_v4_nuke.  We can't hold the lock while calling to tcp_done(), so we drop it before calling. We then have to start at the top of the chain again.  Signed-off-by: Dima Zavin &lt;dima@android.com&gt;  net: ipv4: Fix race in tcp_v4_nuke_addr().  To fix a recursive deadlock in 2.6.29, we stopped holding the hash table lock across tcp_done() calls. This fixed the deadlock, but introduced a race where the socket could die or change state.  Fix: Before unlocking the hash table, we grab a reference to the socket. We can then unlock the hash table without risk of the socket going away. We then lock the socket, which is safe because it is pinned. We can then call tcp_done() without recursive deadlock and without race. Upon return, we unlock the socket and then unpin it, killing it.  Old-Change-Id: Idcdae072b48238b01bdbc8823b60310f1976e045 Signed-off-by: Robert Love &lt;rlove@google.com&gt; Acked-by: Dima Zavin &lt;dima@android.com&gt;  ipv4: disable bottom halves around call to tcp_done().  Signed-off-by: Robert Love &lt;rlove@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Colin Cross &lt;ccross@android.com&gt;  ipv4: Move sk_error_report inside bh_lock_sock in tcp_v4_nuke_addr  When sk_error_report is called, it wakes up the user-space thread, which then calls tcp_close.  When the tcp_close is interrupted by the tcp_v4_nuke_addr ioctl thread running tcp_done, it leaks 392 bytes and triggers a WARN_ON.  This patch moves the call to sk_error_report inside the bh_lock_sock, which matches the locking used in tcp_v4_err.  Change-Id: I34614f7b393182f65091b7a5f19ffa7776c2c575 Signed-off-by: Colin Cross &lt;ccross@android.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423136 Commit-Ready: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423136" owner_email="abhishekbh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/36/423136/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I796b3c7b4a1a7fa35fba9e5192a4a403eb6e17de" commit="bf535367ce8e8de0e8fe35c5aa3e2cefb94fd794" commit_message="net: fix iterating over hashtable in tcp_nuke_addr()  The actual size of the tcp hashinfo table is tcp_hashinfo.ehash_mask + 1 so we need to adjust the loop accordingly to get the sockets hashed into the last bucket.  Change-Id: I796b3c7b4a1a7fa35fba9e5192a4a403eb6e17de Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423137 Commit-Ready: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423137" owner_email="abhishekbh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/37/423137/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I07c70d9a60b125b1070ff05c4eec27daee1a3e90" commit="33fbcdb6a1b5339a78abe10497b5fb9c623634fa" commit_message="net: fix crash in tcp_nuke_addr()  When iterating through sockets we need to skip sockets in TIME_WAIT state as they use lightweight structure inet_timewait_sock that does not have sk_lock member, and if we try to lock them we'll crash thusly:  [   89.376383] BUG: spinlock lockup suspected on CPU#0, netd/431 [   89.382139]  lock: 0xffffffc039d05070, .magic: 66d30606, .owner: /-1682098992, .owner_cpu: 0 [   89.390598] CPU: 0 PID: 431 Comm: netd Tainted: G     U  W 3.18.0 #5 [   89.397389] Hardware name: Google Tegra210 Smaug Rev 1+ (DT) [   89.403049] Call trace: [   89.405501] [&lt;ffffffc0002072b4&gt;] dump_backtrace+0x0/0x10c [   89.410918] [&lt;ffffffc0002073d0&gt;] show_stack+0x10/0x1c [   89.415971] [&lt;ffffffc000a88608&gt;] dump_stack+0x74/0x94 [   89.421018] [&lt;ffffffc000257e8c&gt;] spin_dump+0x78/0x88 [   89.425984] [&lt;ffffffc0002580d8&gt;] do_raw_spin_lock+0xfc/0x158 [   89.431666] [&lt;ffffffc000a90090&gt;] _raw_spin_lock+0x34/0x44 [   89.437059] [&lt;ffffffc0009509a8&gt;] tcp_nuke_addr+0x1fc/0x29c [   89.442548] [&lt;ffffffc0009735f4&gt;] devinet_ioctl+0x288/0x680 [   89.448053] [&lt;ffffffc000975004&gt;] inet_ioctl+0xc4/0xf4 [   89.453103] [&lt;ffffffc0008baedc&gt;] sock_do_ioctl+0x2c/0x5c [   89.458408] [&lt;ffffffc0008bbb54&gt;] sock_ioctl+0x210/0x230 [   89.463633] [&lt;ffffffc000317088&gt;] do_vfs_ioctl+0x4ac/0x590 [   89.469049] [&lt;ffffffc0003171c8&gt;] SyS_ioctl+0x5c/0x88  (or with NULL pointer dereference if lockdep is still working).  Change-Id: I07c70d9a60b125b1070ff05c4eec27daee1a3e90 Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423138 Commit-Ready: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423138" owner_email="abhishekbh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/38/423138/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ied391ef57198175d5c0cd06d5547cab061ffab29" commit="d5e5c3dc21c98ddc4195ccfe0f0e7c90662f728f" commit_message="tcp: Fix IPV6 module build errors  If CONFIG_IPV6=m is selected, we are getting following build errors.  net/built-in.o: In function `tcp_is_local6': net/ipv4/tcp.c:3261: undefined reference to `rt6_lookup'  Making the code conditional upon only CONFIG_IPV6=y fixes this issue.  Also export tcp_nuke_addr to build IPv6 modules. Otherwise we run into following build error:    CC [M]  lib/zlib_deflate/deftree.o   CC [M]  lib/zlib_deflate/deflate_syms.o   LD [M]  lib/zlib_deflate/zlib_deflate.o   Building modules, stage 2.   MODPOST 46 modules ERROR: &quot;tcp_nuke_addr&quot; [net/ipv6/ipv6.ko] undefined! make[2]: *** [__modpost] Error 1  Change-Id: Ied391ef57198175d5c0cd06d5547cab061ffab29 Signed-off-by: Tushar Behera &lt;tushar.behera@linaro.org&gt; CC: John Stultz &lt;john.stultz@linaro.org&gt; Signed-off-by: John Stultz &lt;john.stultz@linaro.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Amit Pundir &lt;amit.pundir@linaro.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423139 Commit-Ready: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="423139" owner_email="abhishekbh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/39/423139/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I4f0145467e5e565cf4c3c8e24e79087a956eccc5" commit="c62851b5f1900e1ffa7e31924cc286d188f6b351" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: tcp: Only perform IPv6 functions is IPv6 is built-in  Build error with IPv6 built as module:  net/built-in.o: In function `tcp_is_local6': net/ipv4/tcp.c:3156: undefined reference to `rt6_lookup'  Alternative would be to define IPV6 as boolean, but that causes trouble elsewhere.  Fixes: c7c3ec4903d3 (&quot;net: socket ioctl to reset connections matching local address&quot;) BUG=chromium:583462 TEST=None (build)  Original-Change-Id: I98ef6d237b79355004ffdc223bce2e23fe368437 Change-Id: I4f0145467e5e565cf4c3c8e24e79087a956eccc5 Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;linux@roeck-us.net&gt; Signed-off-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344368 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423140 Commit-Ready: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423140" owner_email="abhishekbh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/40/423140/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I51d2b29ea7b3206ebbce969a121d11a2e7947cf2" commit="7afef130e02e38984b5bd9e764aec86e52d1a939" commit_message="CHROMIUM: net: tcp: Export tcp_nuke_addr  Otherwise compilation may fail if IPv6 is built as module.  ERROR: &quot;tcp_nuke_addr&quot; [net/ipv6/ipv6.ko] undefined!  Fixes: c7c3ec4903d3 (&quot;net: socket ioctl to reset connections matching local address&quot;) BUG=chromium:583462 TEST=None (build)  Original-Change-Id: Ib18a74aa251cfd3674aa152442a52552e59123b3 Change-Id: I51d2b29ea7b3206ebbce969a121d11a2e7947cf2 Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;linux@roeck-us.net&gt; Signed-off-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/344369 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423141 Commit-Ready: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423141" owner_email="abhishekbh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/41/423141/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Id1431ac457b104252b60e8d171e01724b52b5a91" commit="8250deedbdad243625e5f862eb28a94afa2a150c" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Add more sanity checks to tcp_nuke_addr()  Currently this function will nuke connections in other namespaces, and it will nuke connections even if the socket type does not match. This allows guest OSes running in containers to crea unwanted interference with the host OS.  BUG=b:29515384 TEST=`android-sh -c &quot;ip -6 addr add fc00::1/128 dev arc0; ip -6 addr del fc00::1/128 dev arc0&quot;`  Change-Id: Id1431ac457b104252b60e8d171e01724b52b5a91 Signed-off-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354087 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423142 Commit-Ready: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423142" owner_email="abhishekbh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/42/423142/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I47be2a35a358d9f4e5e79623b639a84c84bb522d" commit="6d1413545076f943703cf43408004044256ac25b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Refactor tcp_nuke_addr() matching logic  This code needs to meet the following requirements:   - Match both &quot;native&quot; IPv4 sockets and IPv6-mapped-IPv4 sockets    (currently the latter sockets are ignored, and Android uses them    extensively).   - Don't nuke connections on loopback interfaces.  Currently this logic    is broken, because tcp_is_local() always returns true.  This happens    because it uses the routing code, which always sends packets destined    for local interfaces through lo:          # ip route get 100.107.2.11         local 100.107.2.11 via ??? ??? dev lo  src 100.107.2.11     Instead, the code will explicly check whether the local address is in    the loopback range.   - As a quirk of how ADB and CTS work under Chrome OS, the ADB port    (5555/tcp) must be excluded from nuking to avoid failing tests.    An explicit check is added for this condition, per b/31635190.  BUG=b:30261109 TEST=`nuketest 0.0.0.0` and see whether it resets IPv4, mapped IPv4, or      IPv6 connections TEST=`nuketest 0.0.0.1` TEST=`nuketest ::` TEST=`nuketest ::1`  Change-Id: I47be2a35a358d9f4e5e79623b639a84c84bb522d Signed-off-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/407923 Reviewed-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/423143 Commit-Ready: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Abhishek Bhardwaj &lt;abhishekbh@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="423143" owner_email="abhishekbh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/43/423143/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" c